From 7cf5a7c3615952b30a08bb190d3d78a68a1d667a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas DeTello <no-reply@detello.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:49:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] platform/x86: acer-wmi: Expose the PT516-52s keyboard
 backlight timeout

The PT516-52s firmware turns the keyboard backlight off after an idle
period, 30 seconds by default. Lighting changes are then invisible until
a key is pressed.

The timeout is reached through the WMID_GUID3 interface already used for
the communication devices. Method 2 (get) takes four bytes: function
number 1, the keyboard backlight hotkey number and 0x08 in byte 2. It
returns eight bytes: error code and EC status in bytes 0 and 1, the
backlight level in byte 4 and the timeout in seconds in byte 5. Method 1
(set) takes eight bytes with the same layout, function number 2 and the
level and timeout in bytes 4 and 5, and returns the two status bytes. A
timeout of 0 means the backlight is never turned off when idle. The
layout matches the Linuwu-Sense, OpenSense and ASense projects, and the
BIOS V1.04 MOF defines the input and output sizes.

The hotkey number, 0x84, is taken from a model quirk. It appears in this
machine's SMBIOS type 170 records, but type_aa_dmi_decode() only reads
the table header, and the record layout has been checked on this model
only.

Add a kbd_backlight_timeout attribute on the platform device, in seconds
from 0 to 255, registered through the driver's attribute groups and
visible when the quirk provides a hotkey and WMID_GUID3 is present. A
write reads the current level first so it is preserved, and accesses are
serialized. Reads always query the firmware, and firmware errors and
malformed replies are returned to userspace as errors. The driver writes
the timeout only when userspace asks: nothing is set at probe or
restored on removal. Document the ABI and add the file to the acer-wmi
MAINTAINERS entry.

Assisted-by: LLM
